{
  "title": "NMOS current mirror",
  "group": "Electronics — analog",
  "description": "NMOS current mirror: diode-connected MN1 sets ~0.2 mA reference, MN2 mirrors it; sweep the output voltage to see the flat current-source characteristic, stepped mirror ratio W2/W1 = 0.5/1/2",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 40,
        "y": -173,
        "title": "NMOS current mirror — what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "Diode-connected MN1 (gate tied to drain) sinks the",
          "reference current set by RREF = 18 kohm from VDD = 5 V,",
          "so IREF ~ (VDD - VGS)/RREF ~ 0.2 mA. MN1 and MN2 share",
          "the same gate and grounded source, so MN2 copies MN1's",
          "VGS and mirrors that current.",
          "",
          "VOUT sweeps MN2's drain 0 -> 5 V. iout is flat once MN2",
          "saturates (VOUT > Vov) -- that flat level is the mirrored",
          "current, and its slight upward slope is the finite output",
          "resistance from lambda. iref (probe on MN1's source) stays",
          "put as a reference. 1-ohm sense resistors turn each branch",
          "current into a probe voltage (iout ~ V/1ohm).",
          "",
          "MN2.W is stepped 0.5x / 1x / 2x of MN1.W, so iout lands at",
          "~0.1 / 0.2 / 0.4 mA -- the mirror ratio is W2/W1.",
          "",
          "Set RREF.R = 9000 and re-run to double IREF (~0.4 mA)."
        ]
      }
    ],
